{# ## Phase 0 — Security & Foundations
   **Status:** [ ] Not started

   **Done when:** Auth works end-to-end, secrets are gitignored, RBAC
   middleware rejects unauthorized requests, all Phase 0 security items pass.

   ### Security checklist (non-negotiable — must finish before Phase 1)
   - [ ] `.env` in `.gitignore`, `.env.example` committed with placeholder values
   - [ ] Secrets never hard-coded; loaded only via settings/config module
   - [ ] JWT signing key is randomly generated (≥ 256 bits), never committed
   - [ ] Passwords hashed with bcrypt (cost ≥ 12) — never stored in plaintext
   - [ ] Auth endpoints rate-limited (e.g. 10 req/min per IP)
   - [ ] RBAC middleware in place; all protected routes return 401/403 correctly
   - [ ] Input validation on all user-supplied fields (Pydantic / Zod schema)
   - [ ] CORS restricted to known origins (no wildcard in production)

   ### Tasks
   - [ ] Initialize repo, set up pyproject.toml / package.json, commit baseline
   - [ ] Configure environment variable loading (pydantic-settings / dotenv)
   - [ ] Create database schema + initial Alembic migration
   - [ ] Implement JWT auth (issue, verify, refresh, revoke)
   - [ ] Implement RBAC middleware (role checked on every protected route)
   - [ ] Write smoke tests: register → login → protected route → 401 without token
   - [ ] Update workplan ✅
#}

